{# The form above a table of the account (architecture §5.2): what the table is narrowed to, in a form a
   browser sends with no script, and the way back to the table as it opens. Each table names what narrows
   it in the block "fields", the days of a period (account/filter_period) and the choices of a word
   (account/filter_choice), and passes "narrowed", whether it is read otherwise than it opens.

   The page is not carried over: a filter that changed is a table read from its first page, which is why
   the form posts to the route alone and the control under the table is the only thing that names a page.
   What the fields hold is what was read and not what the request said: a period that ends before it
   starts, or a word the table does not offer, is read as none.

   The provider ships the shape and the words, never a class: "data-filter" is what a stylesheet reads. #}
{% trans_default_domain 'beffroi' %}
{% set route = app.request.attributes.get('_route') %}
{% set own = app.request.attributes.get('_route_params') ?? {} %}
<form method="get" action="{{ path(route, own) }}" data-filter="table" aria-label="{{ 'filter.label'|trans }}">
    <div data-filter="fields">
        {% block fields %}{% endblock %}
    </div>
    <div data-filter="actions">
        <button type="submit" data-filter="apply">{{ 'filter.apply'|trans }}</button>
        {% if narrowed %}
            <a href="{{ path(route, own) }}" data-filter="clear">{{ 'filter.clear'|trans }}</a>
        {% endif %}
    </div>
</form>
